"""Reviewer-authored coverage; line hashing is bookkeeping, not proof validation."""
from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json,re
H=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
ROOT=H.parents[2]
base=ROOT/'work/quartic-version6-release/repository/manuscripts/quartic_v13.tex'
addition=H.parent/'addition.tex'
def sha(b):return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()
def record(path,start,end,ids,argument,status='reviewed as an inherited supplier interface'):
    lines=path.read_bytes().splitlines(keepends=True)
    return {'file':str(path.relative_to(ROOT)),'file_sha256':sha(path.read_bytes()),
            'start_line':start,'end_line':end,'raw_span_sha256':sha(b''.join(lines[start-1:end])),
            'matched_inventory_ids':ids.split(),'reviewer_argument':argument,'status':status}

# These groups were derived by reading the proof, then reconciled with inventory IDs.
specs=[
(20772,20802,'V13-FINITE-COUNTS V13-SOS-FINITE','The retained theorem states precisely 394 symbolic and 411 ordinary variables, not witnesses. It is a historical theorem; Version14 adds a separate smaller presentation. Its existing exact artifact acceptance is retained, while the new final tables were expanded independently.'),
(20803,20830,'V13-MODEL V13-HEIGHT','The roots and all height scales remain in the same K=Q(sqrt2) model. The height implication requires a nonzero integer N and the powers of all three contact radicals. The all-empty case submits N=1. Version14 restores the integer root domain and anchor before using this interface; it does not extend the height theorem to half-integral root labels.'),
(20831,20901,'V13-LOG-APPROX V13-LOG-TRANSFER','The actual N8/Q2 approximant has relative error40r and absolute log error41r; V1 instead uses error12. Unit extensions at O make zero numerators legitimate. Integrality is transferred before improving primary depth. Version14 independently proves the revised H-depth bootstrap and uses doubled integer group identities for its larger auxiliary domain, so the old doubled-auxiliary hypothesis is not silently reused.'),
(20902,21007,'V13-ODD-NORM V13-SHARED-RECIPROCAL V13-IDENTITY-CHARTS V13-V0-EXCLUSION V13-RECIPROCAL-IDENTITY V13-H-EXACT-RESCALING','The old half-point norm condition fixes the odd squareclass, allowing the second root of the half-point quadratic. Identity-inclusive reciprocal charts use r=0 and g=0 with prescribed zero ratios and handle U=-Q by the regular doubling formula. The common normalizer is -1/z(H), not its negative. V0=O is excluded by a fixed unit and the N=1 height contradiction before an LP denominator is interpreted. Version14 supplies replacement reciprocal charts and explicit new ratio domains, while preserving this supplier logic for H/V0.'),
(21008,21059,'V13-BIQUADRATIC','The three displayed identities recover both conics and the oriented subtraction under c=a^2 and b^2=c^2-D. Division is by nonzero a,c and the old real-positive d,e, never r,g or the output ratios. This is the old witness source for the Version14 forward map; those positivity hypotheses are not transferred to arbitrary newly admitted E(K) auxiliaries.'),
(21060,21156,'V13-H-HALF-INDEX V13-H-TORSION-EXCLUSION V13-H-SUBTRACTION V13-H-NO-ROOT V13-H-LOG-IDENTITIES','The old H chart gives a finite point with nonzero x and excludes E[2] and both +/-P+E[2] using their unit reciprocal abscissae. The explicit subtraction then proves nonzero d,N,Tprime and identifies H-P and ell0. N mod71 and Q mod7 exclude every K-root, with split primes and unit leading coefficients. I repeated those finite checks. All group multipliers are integral; h=m/2 denotes only the free index. Version14 compares the weaker positive H test explicitly and doubles both coefficients when auxiliary torsion is also allowed.'),
(21157,21298,'V13-INPUT-PARITY V13-INPUT-LOCAL-ONE-CHOICE V13-DETERMINISTIC-CORRECTION V13-SCALAR-NORM24 V13-SCALAR-TORSION-LOG V13-SCALAR-HEIGHT V13-ANCHOR-COEFFICIENT','The input bridge needs odd beta, since mere integrality permits X=-1/2. For integral input the local r values and c=r+4896 give square cr at 2,3,17. New support of c is prepared before L. The scalar nested sums have opposite local valuation parity and yield both coefficient depths24. A small z(R) may mean R is near (0,0), so duplication to 2R precedes the logarithm. The unchanged scalar group identity kills H torsion and gives an integral-index divisibility. The exact numerical height margin was repeated. Version14 retains the same oriented S and all scalar consumers.'),
(21299,21317,'V13-HEIGHT-CONTRADICTIONS','The Lucas residual is submitted to the height theorem only if nonzero; contradiction gives its vanishing. The nonzero odd b then supplies log B>|a|-3. The second application uses the nonzero reduced numerator of n-beta and order10, contradicting the scalar bound. Version14 delivers the same integral labels, parity, orders and scalar bound, so the same final argument applies.'),
(21318,21365,'V13-GROUPED-POLYNOMIALS V13-TORIC-POWERS V13-CONSTANT-PIVOT','Old grouped products represent product(1+qY), including conjugation and affine coordinate normalizations. Constant-pivot elimination requires every consumer identity and a nonzero constant pivot. Old toric divisions need nonzero E,q. Version14 does not use these as generic claims about a new grouped detector: it writes and proves its final three groups anew; the exact private power chains retain ER=1.'),
(21366,21402,'V13-FACTORED-POLES V13-PREPARATION-CONIC','The factored second conic pulls back with factor t^2. New solutions reconstruct old ones even at t=0; completeness at t=0 uses semantic positive input to force F=q=0. Stored scalar sign is opposite to semantic sign. The preparation-conic inverse treats b+U=0 separately and preserves only the square N. These inherited pole suppliers apply to Version14 because the new completeness construction re-establishes the same semantic positivity and preparation conditions.'),
(21403,21490,'V13-REAL-INITIAL V13-FINITE-SUPPORT V13-REAL-FINAL-CRT V13-PREPARATION-ZERO','A single ordered choice first selects H0, then a scalar point R with all finite depths and strict real smallness. The support is supp(cr) union {2,3,17}; 17 remains required even outside supp(cr). L and a compact real neighborhood avoiding comparison poles precede contact primes. The positive-tail progression has both residue and modulus divisible by m0. Version14 adds an allowed finite scalar depth before roots are fixed and chooses its private anchor after the contacts, with estimates uniform in gamma/lambda. It does not make incompatible independent choices of H.'),
(21491,21520,'V13-NORMALIZED-SCALAR-POLE','The outside scalar equations prove semantic b=-Kx positive and x nonzero before any private pole normalization. Weight-one and weight-two private slots scale by the corresponding powers of x. Every remaining residual gains x^2; no private zero value is excluded. Version14 retains this scalar subsystem and its sign convention.'),
(21521,21588,'V13-ANCHOR-RESCALING V13-ORDINARY-GATE','The original full-system anchor rescaling first uses the nonzero even scalar index to prove F=2g0g1 nonzero, so it is not an isolated-anchor equivalence at arbitrary g1=0. The old ordinary companion needs16 constant gates plus C*tau. Version14 instead restores parity from the shifted anchor and uses its exact unscaled anchor plus14 weighted constant gates and a root-sum gate. The old17-gate accounting is retained only for P411.'),
(21589,21607,'V13-FINAL-COMPLETENESS','The old completeness proof selects one final H satisfying every finite and real requirement and supplies fresh poles. It does not assert that arbitrary old poles survive a changed logarithm or scalar input. Version14 uses this choice order, the original Pi19 progression and its own changed detector/anchor completeness proof.'),
(21608,21632,'V13-SOS-FINITE V13-FINITE-COUNTS','The old polynomial is exactly the sum of364 normalized quadratic residual squares and its ordinary companion has381. Over Q the simultaneous zero set agrees with that sum. Existing artifact identity and prior acceptance cover these historical counts; new299/314 tables have separate independent full expansions and actual-coordinate checks.'),
(21633,22075,'','Bibliography and TeX separation contain source identities and version qualifications, not additional inferential proof steps. I read all entries. The identities relevant here include Silverman second edition and Voight corrected online v1.0.7u, plus internal supplier passages whose underlying sources are reviewed in the other baseline partitions. Existing qualifications about preprints, inaccessible typeset editions, corrections and source dates remain; a listed bibliography item does not constitute acceptance of every theorem in that work.'),
(22076,22087,'','The AI usage statement and document end are provenance and TeX structure, not a mathematical premise. It explicitly distinguishes internal model review from independent human peer review. This review makes the same distinction.')]

rows=[record(base,a,b,ids,arg,'nonproof provenance/source-identity record' if not ids else 'reviewed inherited application and current dependency effect') for a,b,ids,arg in specs]
assert [i for a,b,_,_ in specs for i in range(a,b+1)]==list(range(20772,22088))
inventory=ROOT/'work/quartic-version6-release/repository/docs/manuscript-revisions/version13/APPLICATIONS.json'
ids=set(json.loads(inventory.read_bytes())['applicationIds'])
assert set(x for r in rows for x in r['matched_inventory_ids'])==ids
data={'reviewer':'/root/astra_v14_source_review','scope':'Baseline lines20772–22087 and their dependency effects in Version14; original earlier arithmetic suppliers are inherited, not newly proved here.',
      'initial_discovery':'INITIAL-SOURCE-USES.md and INITIAL-SOURCE-HASHES.json preceded inventory reconciliation. The bibliography and final baseline tail were later read fully to complete the parent-assigned partition. R6 exposed application names before the final old-inventory comparison; no claim of blind independence from those names is made.',
      'baseline_inventory_sha256':sha(inventory.read_bytes()),'coverage':rows,
      'all_39_baseline_application_ids_matched':True,
      'current_addition_sha256':sha(addition.read_bytes()),
      'status':'Reviewer coverage; final current-manuscript acceptance is separately hash-bound.'}
(H/'BASELINE-COVERAGE.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
new_specs=[
('N48-ORDINARY-CORRECTED299','The numerical theorem distinguishes total variables from witnesses and the fixed symbolic C from a quantified coordinate. Both final SOS polynomials, compact maps and decimal texts were independently reconstructed. The compact/source-ID byte counts are now separately stated.'),
('','The K-model, root labels, three physical scales and pre-H height/anchor interface are explicit. These are inherited theorem suppliers, not conclusions from the finite compiler. The following sections restore the precise hypotheses before consuming them.'),
('N01-KUMMER-AFFINE N02-SQUARED-H-RECONSTRUCTION N03-SQUARED-H-EXCEPTIONS','The affine H equations exclude f=0 without height. The inverse certificate divides only by c*f; the old forward direction uses its proved exceptional-point exclusion. The squared presentation reconstructs on UQ nonzero and explicitly classifies U=0 and Q=0, including both fixed values. Its later local argument excludes those branches before the reconstruction is used.'),
('N07-S-PARITY N08-S-HALF-RESTORATION N15-ABSCISSA-COEFFICIENTS N16-SHIFTED-ANCHOR359 N17-ROOT-SIGN-RESTORATION N18-EXACT-UNSCALING','The squareclass proof first gives integral root labels. The scalar subtraction treats both equal-abscissa cases before defining Fs. The 3-adic leading coefficient and separate ramified2-adic coefficient calculation have their actual uses separated. Disjoint valuations recover original anchor integrality and oddness without assuming either. Complete sign actions preserve physical points and the oriented S scalar input. The explicit unscaling identities restore every private anchor equation, including zero private values.'),
('N04-CONTACT-POLE-LOCAL N05-CONTACT-POLE-COMPLETE N06-CONDITIONAL-GUARDS','The R and E here are the physical contact polynomial and its inverse. Trace and pole quotients are interpreted only at required odd positive contacts after nonzero W. Radical-free detectors need no inverse or excluded R=-1 branch. The square multiplier relating to the old contact function preserves chosen support, and the new pole denominator contributes only even valuations.'),
('N09-PREH-VALUATION-AND-CACHE N13-THREE326-LOCAL N24-COMMON-SCALE-LOCAL','The final groups have explicitly defined physical powers and conjugation. Pre-log even valuations follow from the point cubics or the classified signed H branches. Their nonzero residue classes give one common successful place through the trace/pole inequality. The gamma guard and alpha=1,3,>=5 cases yield the claimed bounds. In response to review the text now explicitly applies the EU low test to the old H fixed-point unit obstruction; no old order40 hypothesis is silently reused.'),
('N36-AUXILIARY-ALL-E-VALUATIONS N37-ZERO-SAFE-RAW-RATIOS N40-ORIENTED-RECIPROCAL-CLOSURE N41-ROOT-RESTORATION-AND-COMPLETENESS N43-ALTERNATE-ORDINATE-RECONSTRUCTION N44-RAW-RATIO-GLOBAL-REDUNDANCY N45-S-ORIENTED-RECIPROCAL-EXTENSION N46-S-ALL-E-DOMAIN-APPLICATION N47-S-CACHE-REPAIR-BINDING','The negative reciprocal ordinate is fixed. Polynomial restoration gives both cubics and the complete slope closure before local analysis. The secant, equal-abscissa tangent and both identity endpoints recover U-V with the displayed ordinate. The literal height-product chain excludes c=0. S retains a,b,c with its additional orientation equation and the correct196/197 cache. N0 is now explicitly the existing affine normalizer before H semantics. The missing raw alternate ratio is recovered only after low tests show 1-DB locally a unit; identity branches give coefficient1. This is a full-system argument, not a generic conic cancellation.'),
('N25-H-DEPTH-BOOTSTRAP N38-AUXILIARY-TORSION-LOG-TRANSFER N39-GLOBAL-APPROXIMANT-DOMAIN','The points lie in E(K), while roots remain in2E(K). Doubling both coefficients in the integral identities kills both torsion terms. Half-indices are only locally integral, which suffices. Depth-one units first transfer integrality; F(0,0,0)=-1 then forces a unit primary ratio and H depth10. Only afterward are errors40/12/40 used. Identity numerators have zero error. The global no-root certificates replace the invalid enlarged-domain real positivity shortcut. The scalar application consumes the unchanged oriented point.'),
('N14-THREE326-COMPLETE N26-COMMON-SCALE-COMPLETE','The original Pi19 construction supplies primary depth20 and actual middle precision12. Contact margins are positive. All eight changed coefficient forms have positive small-prime slopes and negative real exponents, uniformly for gamma/lambda in(1,2). Root/scalar data and compact neighborhoods precede contacts; gamma precedes the final H. Extra gamma primes create only even pole valuations outside contact support.'),
('N29-ANCHOR-GAMMA-CHAIN N30-ANCHOR-SMALL-LOCAL N31-ANCHOR-CONTACT-LOCAL N32-ANCHOR-RATIONAL-APPROXIMATION N33-ANCHOR-COMPLETE-ORDER','The eight gates force u nonzero and reconstruct old gamma exactly, giving soundness. Completeness uses the same quadric Q=N, with N nonzero and an inherited rational basepoint. Extra scalar dyadic depth gives odd t. Each stated local point at2,3,17 and contact primes satisfies the exact quadric; contact denominators are excluded before selecting primes. The line map reaches the complement of its tangent section, and the explicit local curve leaves that section even at P. CRT with adjustable denominators approximates all three directions and the real interval. These are existence proof parameters, not uncounted quartic variables.'),
('N12-CHAIN327 N20-EXACT-LAURENT-CHAIN N27-SPARSE-SHARED314 N40-ORIENTED-RECIPROCAL-CLOSURE N41-ROOT-RESTORATION-AND-COMPLETENESS N43-ALTERNATE-ORDINATE-RECONSTRUCTION','The old reciprocal witnesses give f,h,F,k by explicit rational formulas, including identity values. The actual group equality supplies a finite chord/tangent slope with no new point choice. Exact ordinate deletion, local Laurent power recovery and sparse Lucas recentering preserve their stated consumers. Arithmetic detector changes are not mislabeled as fiber bijections. The final279-row unweighted primitive SOS was independently expanded into the exact6630-term table.'),
('N48-ORDINARY-CORRECTED299','The14 output-linear gates have unique values with final exponent2^25. The added root-sum coordinate prevents a cubic C times root-square term. Exactly rows504/1903 change; substitution recovers both literal symbolic rows, and all other299 coordinates and277 rows remain. The independently expanded294-row SOS has6672 monomials and a6496-bit maximum. Compact reindexing fixes the distinguished input through the explicit map.')]
line_count=len(addition.read_bytes().splitlines())
starts=[1]+[i for i,l in enumerate(addition.read_text().splitlines(),1) if l.startswith('\\subsection')]
assert len(starts)==len(new_specs)
